commit 238ef9f33cf3df9b390fad13959e48410ec26947
Author: Mazin Fadl <mazen@illumed.net>
Date:   Sat Oct 24 13:31:18 2026 -0400

    db: use notmuch_database_open_with_config()
    
    notmuch_database_open() is deprecated since libnotmuch 5.4 (notmuch 0.32).
    Open the database with notmuch_database_open_with_config(), passing the
    notmuch config path astroid resolved, so the library's configuration matches
    the ptree astroid reads its settings from.
    
    Database location discovery now mirrors the documented notmuch search order
    (notmuch-config(5), DATABASE LOCATION): NOTMUCH_DATABASE, database.path,
    $XDG_DATA_HOME/notmuch/$PROFILE, $MAILDIR, $HOME/mail. A location is
    accepted in either on-disk form: the database directory itself (xapian/ — the
    XDG profile layout, and database.path when database.mail_root is set) or a
    mail root (.notmuch/xapian). database.mail_root is the mail store root, not a
    database location.
    
    Open failures now log notmuch's error message and the path tried.
    
    cmake requires notmuch_database_open_with_config (libnotmuch >= 5.4) at
    configure time. The tests require NOTMUCH_CONFIG (set by tests/run_test.sh)
    instead of guessing a config path.

